  <section id="s-stages" data-code="stages">
    <div class="section-no">01 — Pipeline Lifecycle</div>
    <h2>Bird's-Eye View of the LLM Lifecycle</h2>
    <p>Building a frontier large language model is no longer a matter of simply scraping web text and running a next-token prediction transformer. Modern models undergo a highly structured, sequential multi-stage training pipeline. Each stage serves a specific purpose, shifting the model's capacity from generic language understanding to targeted domain recall, formatting layout compliance, and deep, multi-step self-correcting reasoning.</p>
    <p>The transition moves through four key phases: **Pre-Training** (ingesting raw web tokens), **Mid-Training** (extending context length and code/math specialty), **Supervised Fine-Tuning** (teaching layout syntax and thinking characteristics), and finally **Reinforcement Learning** (using verifiable environments to drive step-by-step logic expansion). Understanding this sequence is vital to seeing how a modern reasoning agent is built.</p>
    
    <div class="vp">
